&lt;h2 id="v141"&gt;v1.4.1
&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;v1.4.1&lt;/code&gt; is a maintenance release focused on metric accuracy and RPM upgrade compatibility.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>PG Exporter 1.4 Documentation</title><link>https://pigsty.io/docs/pg_exporter/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://pigsty.io/docs/pg_exporter/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;The ultimate monitoring experience for PostgreSQL with &lt;strong&gt;600+ metrics&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;declarative configuration&lt;/strong&gt;, and &lt;strong&gt;dynamic planning&lt;/strong&gt; capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://pigsty.io/docs/pg_exporter/start"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Get Started&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href="https://github.com/pgsty/pg_exporter"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GitHub&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href="https://g.pgsty.com"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Live Demo&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2 id="features"&gt;Features
&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class="td-table-scroll td-table-scroll--static"&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
 &lt;thead&gt;
 &lt;tr&gt;
 &lt;th scope="col"&gt;Feature&lt;/th&gt;
 &lt;th scope="col"&gt;Description&lt;/th&gt;
 &lt;/tr&gt;
 &lt;/thead&gt;
 &lt;tbody&gt;
 &lt;tr&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Comprehensive Metrics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;600+ metrics covering nearly every statistics view of PostgreSQL (10-19+) and pgBouncer (1.8-1.25+)&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;/tr&gt;
 &lt;tr&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Declarative Collectors&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;Every metric comes from a YAML collector definition — a SQL query plus execution conditions; add, change, or remove metrics without touching code&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;/tr&gt;
 &lt;tr&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dynamic Planning&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;Each collector branch is admitted per target based on version, primary/replica role, installed extensions, and tags&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;/tr&gt;
 &lt;tr&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Auto-Discovery&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;Automatically discovers and scrapes every database in an instance, distinguished by the &lt;code&gt;datname&lt;/code&gt; label&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;/tr&gt;
 &lt;tr&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Health Check APIs&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;/up&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;/primary&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;/replica&lt;/code&gt; endpoints serve directly as load-balancer probes for primary/replica traffic routing&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;/tr&gt;
 &lt;tr&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Smart Caching&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;Per-collector TTL caching decouples scrape frequency from query frequency — probe and scrape storms never reach the database&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;/tr&gt;
 &lt;tr&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Snapshot Histograms&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;HISTOGRAM&lt;/code&gt; column type aggregates SQL snapshots into classic Prometheus histogram distributions&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;/tr&gt;
 &lt;tr&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Extension Aware&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;Native support for pg_stat_statements, pg_wait_sampling, citus, and timescaledb&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;/tr&gt;
 &lt;tr&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Production Ready&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;Battle-tested in real-world environments across 12K+ cores for 6+ years&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;/tr&gt;
 &lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2 id="version-info"&gt;Version Info
&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Current stable release: &lt;a href="https://github.com/pgsty/pg_exporter/releases/tag/v1.4.1"&gt;&lt;code&gt;v1.4.1&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Default config support: PostgreSQL &lt;strong&gt;10-19+&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Legacy config support: PostgreSQL &lt;strong&gt;9.1-9.6&lt;/strong&gt; via the &lt;code&gt;legacy/&lt;/code&gt; config bundle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;pgBouncer support: &lt;strong&gt;1.8-1.25+&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;See &lt;a href="https://pigsty.io/docs/pg_exporter/release"&gt;Release Notes&lt;/a&gt; for the full history.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>